प्र-भङ्ग, अस्, आ, अम्, Ved. breaking, crushing;
(अस्), m. breaking, crushing, destroying, destruction,
complete defeat.

प्र-भेद, अस्, m. splitting, cutting through;
division, separation, distinction, difference, disparity;
kind, sort; the flowing of a juice or peculiar fluid
from the temples of an elephant; [cf. 2. दान,
p. 408, col. 1.]

प्रभुज् 2. प्र-भुज् (see rt. 2. भुज्), cl. 7. P.
A. -भुनक्ति, -भुङ्क्ते, -भोक्तुम्, to begin to eat;
to protect, govern (?).

प्र-भवन, अम्, n. production, source, origin;
the being born or produced; ruling, presiding (?);
(अस्, आ, अम्), produced from, springing from (at the
end of a comp.; cf. मेरु-प्˚).

प्र-भव्य, अस्, आ, अम्, to be born or produced;
being at the source or origin, original; fit for
rule (?).

प्रभूष् प्र-भूष्, cl. 1. P. -भूषति, -भू-
षितुम्, Ved. to set forth in order; to offer, present;
(Sāy.) = प्रकर्षेण स्वी-कृ.

प्रभ्रम् प्र-भ्रम्, cl. 1. 4. P. -भ्रमति,
-भ्राम्यति, -भ्रमितुम्, to roam or wander about;
to roam or wander through.
